ood","inaccuracy","best","good","best","good","best","best","best","forced","best","mistake","best","best","forced","best","great","best","forced","best","best","best","best","best","excellent","best","excellent","excellent","best","best","best","best","best","best","excellent","excellent","best","best","best","best","good","good","excellent","best","good","best","best","best","best","excellent","best","best","best","excellent","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best"],"moments":[{"ply":51,"name":"26.c4","cls":"mistake","color":"w","headline":"26.c4 is a mistake: White's winning chances go from 40% to 24%.","points":["Black answers 26…Rh8: the rook takes the open h-file.","Better was 26.Qd3 (−1.15)."],"better":"26.Qd3 prepares Ra1 and c4. After 26…Rxe1+ 27.Rxe1 Qxd3 28.cxd3 a5 29.Ra1, the rooks are traded and the queens come off (−1.15)."},{"ply":54,"name":"27…Rh8","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"27…Rh8! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The rook takes the open h-file.","The rook joins the attack: it now hits 2 squares around the White king.","The next best move, 27…b6, would drop Black's winning chances from 73% to 60% (−1.10).","27…Rh8 stops c5 and takes the open h-file.","White was threatening c5, winning a pawn, picking it up with 28.cxd6. Rh8 takes care of it.","White answers 28.Qe3."]},{"ply":56,"name":"28…g4","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"28…g4! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["A pawn break: it challenges the f3 pawn to open lines.","Pushes a pawn towards the White king, to pry open lines in front of it.","The next best move, 28…Qh7, would drop Black's winning chances from 82% to 64% (−1.52).","28…g4 threatens …gxf3, winning two pawns.","It threatens …gxf3, winning two pawns, so White has to spend the next move on it.","White answers 29.fxg4, taking the g4 pawn and pushing the pawn storm towards the king, leaving Black with an isolated pawn on f6."]},{"ply":59,"name":"30.Rf1","cls":"mistake","color":"w","headline":"30.Rf1 is a mistake: White's winning chances go from 25% to 13%.","points":["Black answers 30…Bxg2, which takes the pawn on g2.","Better was 30.Qf2 (−2.99): adds a decisive attacker on the f6 pawn: 2 attackers against 1 defender."],"better":"30.Qf2 threatens Qxf6+, with mate in 7, and stops …Bxg2. After 30…Rh6 31.c3 Rg6 32.Qe2 Qxg2+ 33.Qxg2 Rxg2+ 34.Kf1, the queens come off and White is a pawn down (−2.99)."},{"ply":60,"name":"30…Rh6","cls":"miss","color":"b","headline":"30…Rh6 misses the chance 30.Rf1 gave: 30…Bxg2 would have punished it. Black's winning chances go from 87% to 69%.","points":["White answers 31.Rf2: shores up the g2 pawn, which was under as much attack as it had defence (2 against 2).","The rook on h6 can be taken by the queen on d2.","Better was 30…Bxg2 (−5.20), which takes the pawn on g2."],"better":"30…Bxg2 threatens …Rh1+, with mate in 3. Engine line: 31.Rxf6+ Ke7 32.Qxg2 Qd1+ 33.Rf1 Qxd4+ 34.Rf2 (−5.20)."},{"ply":86,"name":"43…Qxb4+","cls":"mistake","color":"b","headline":"43…Qxb4+ is a mistake: Black's winning chances go from 69% to 50%.","points":["White answers 44.Kd1: the king steps out of check to d1.","Better was 43…Qc3+ (−2.18): the queen forks the king and the pawn: both can't be saved at once."],"better":"43…Qc3+ wins a pawn, picking it up with 44…Qxc2+, and forks the king and the pawn. After 44.Kf2 Qxc2+ 45.Ke3 Qc1+ 46.Kf2 Qd2+, Black comes out a pawn up (−2.18)."},{"ply":91,"name":"46.Bb8","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"46.Bb8! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Moves the attacked bishop to safety.","The next best move, 46.Qb8, would drop White's winning chances from 49% to 20% (−3.73).","46.Bb8 gets the bishop out of the way of …Kxa7.","Black was threatening …Kxa7, winning a bishop. The bishop steps away.","Black answers 46…Qe1+, giving check, leaving one reply.","After 46…Qe1+ 47.Kb2 Qe5+ 48.Qc3 b5 49.Qxe5 dxe5 50.Kb3, the queens come off (0.00)."]}],"opening":{"name":"Italian Game: Two Knights Defense, Modern Bishop's Opening","eco":"C55","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 6…g6: 12 moves in all, 6 by White and 6 by Black.","Theory runs out after 6…g6: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}